WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:03.869
-Well, here we are, everybody.
Election day is tomorrow,

00:00:03.869 --> 00:00:06.105
and the president has settled
on his closing message --

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:07.940
promising to fire
Dr. Anthony Fauci

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.376
and threatening to prematurely
declare victory

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:11.978
and steal the election
through the courts.

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:14.313
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:14.313 --> 00:00:18.384 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:19.752
We're in the midst
of the worst stretch

00:00:19.752 --> 00:00:21.521
of the coronavirus outbreak
since it began,

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:24.123
And the bleak reality will only
get bleaker.

00:00:24.123 --> 00:00:26.259
With as many as a thousand
Americans dying a day,

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:29.496
and nearly 100,000 new cases
recorded on Friday alone,

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:31.363
the nation is crying out
for leadership.

00:00:31.363 --> 00:00:33.599
And with just one day left in
the most consequential election

00:00:33.599 --> 00:00:35.134
Of our lifetimes, the president

00:00:35.134 --> 00:00:37.436
has finally settled
on his closing message.

00:00:37.436 --> 00:00:39.906
-Like the great Pavarotti, the
singer, when --

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:41.741
you know, he was a very --
he was diva.

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.142
He was the greatest
of all divas.

00:00:43.142 --> 00:00:47.046
He was an incredible talent with
the most unbelievable voice.

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:50.283
And I've gone to concerts
where he would say,

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:52.718
"No, no, no, no,
I do not feel good.

00:00:52.718 --> 00:00:55.421
I will not sing tonight,"
and he'd leave.

00:00:55.421 --> 00:00:57.056
See? And then I've gone
to somewhere,

00:00:57.056 --> 00:01:00.193
it was the most unbelievable
voice that ever lived.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:02.495
I mean, the greatest, right?
Pavarotti.

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:05.064
But he was a -- he liked me,
for whatever reason.

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:07.200
He was very terrible
to other people.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.034
To me, he was nice. He liked me.

00:01:09.034 --> 00:01:11.704
But he goes, "Donald, Donald,
I will not sing tonight."

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:12.872
He'd have a thousand people.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:15.675
"I will not sing tonight because
I not feel --

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:17.844
I will leave tonight."
And he'd leave.

00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:20.480
"Ladies and gentlemen,
he's just canceled."

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.182
But when he was great,
he was great.

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:25.050
-Ah, yes, just what your rally
crowds are interested in --

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:27.487
the entertainment enjoyed
by wealthy New Yorkers.

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:29.788
[ As Trump ] And how about
David Sedaris, folks?

00:01:29.788 --> 00:01:32.959
Oh, we love to read his dry,
whimsical essays

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:34.794
on our decks in Bridgehampton.
You know it?

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:36.128
[ Normal voice ]
What was the thinking

00:01:36.128 --> 00:01:37.497
behind telling that story?

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:39.465
"Mr. President, polling has you
behind in the rust belt."

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:41.467
[ As Trump ] Don't worry.
I'll do my Pavarotti chunk.

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:43.536
[ Normal voice ] Talking about
Pavarotti at a Trump rally

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:46.573
is like holding a Yo-Yo Ma night
at a monster truck rally.

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:47.873
[ Gruff voice ]
Tonight at Watkins Glen,

00:01:47.873 --> 00:01:51.477
say goodbye to Bulldozer and
"cello" to Yo-Yo Monster!

00:01:51.477 --> 00:01:53.246
[ Normal voice ] There's so much
to unpack from that clip.

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:54.413
First, I love how Trump says,

00:01:54.413 --> 00:01:55.915
"But he liked me
for whatever reason,"

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.550
basically admitting that even
Trump doesn't know

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:58.818
why anyone would like him.

00:01:58.818 --> 00:02:01.654
Second, no one swings
more wildly between praise

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:03.389
and criticism faster than Trump,

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:05.859
who says Pavarotti is the
greatest in one breath,

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:08.628
and then he was very terrible
to other people in the next.

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:10.196
[ As Trump ]
Pavarotti, voice of an angel,

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:12.698
heart of a calcified turd.
Just a bad guy.

00:02:12.698 --> 00:02:14.567
Bad, bad guy.

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:16.035
[ Normal voice ] And third,
Trump supporters will follow

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:18.238
Trump anywhere, but even they
had nothing but blank stares

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:20.539
for that one.
"I know Giuliani and Scaramucci.

00:02:20.539 --> 00:02:21.774
Which one is Pavarotti?"

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:24.243
And finally,
was that long-ass story

00:02:24.243 --> 00:02:25.712
Trump telling us if he loses,

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:27.847
he'll just walk away
like Pavarotti?

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:30.482
Eh. Probably wishful thinking.

00:02:30.482 --> 00:02:32.051
He told it because right before

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:33.886
he went on stage,
he saw a pizza box.

00:02:33.886 --> 00:02:36.088
[ As Trump ]
Oh, looks like Pavarotti.

00:02:36.088 --> 00:02:37.156
[ Normal voice ]
This is where Trump is at.

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:38.557
His record is so horrendous,

00:02:38.557 --> 00:02:40.926
he has nothing to talk about
other than rambling incoherently

00:02:40.926 --> 00:02:43.429
about long-dead celebrities who
were nice to him 20 years ago.

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:45.331
In fact, with basically
one day left,

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:48.600
Trump decided that
regaling his crowds

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.604
with bizarre backstage
encounters with opera singers

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:54.073
wasn't enough, so he decided
to close out the campaign

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:55.908
by threatening to fire
the nation's

00:02:55.908 --> 00:02:58.544
top infectious disease expert,
Dr. Anthony Fauci,

00:02:58.544 --> 00:03:01.414
a man whose popularity in polls
far exceeds Trump's.

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:18.564
-Don't tell anybody,
but let me wait

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:21.266
till a little bit
after the election.

00:03:21.266 --> 00:03:23.335
-You're going fire one
of the country's most trusted

00:03:23.335 --> 00:03:24.903
scientists in the middle
of a pandemic?

00:03:24.903 --> 00:03:26.906
Who are you going to replace him
with, zombie Pavarotti?

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:28.741
[ As Trump ] Only the fake news
says he's dead, folks.

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.876
We gave him a shot of Regeneron
right in the ass,

00:03:30.876 --> 00:03:32.412
and now he is good as new.

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:34.414
Luciano, sing a few bars for us.

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:37.884
[ As Pavarotti ] ♪ Brains-ah!
Give me the brains! ♪

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:39.752
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:41.587
[ Normal voice ] I can't believe
this is Trump's closing message

00:03:41.587 --> 00:03:42.821
for the last day
of the campaign.

00:03:42.821 --> 00:03:44.523
Trump says stuff like this
because he doesn't think

00:03:44.523 --> 00:03:46.092
he's accountable
to public opinion.

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:48.027
Remember,
he lost the popular vote,

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:49.695
escaped impeachment,
and has never had

00:03:49.695 --> 00:03:52.198
a majority approval rating
once in his presidency.

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:54.967
He thinks our anti-Democratic
institutions like the Senate

00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:57.203
and the electoral college
and the Supreme Court

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:59.372
will protect him, and he's been
broadcasting as much,

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:01.874
announcing that he'll use
the courts to potentially

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:05.078
steal the election by
prematurely declaring victory

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:06.279
and shutting down the count.

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:08.781
-Axios reported that the
president claims

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:11.150
to declare victory Tuesday night

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:14.353
if he appears to be "ahead."

00:04:14.353 --> 00:04:17.457
Of course, some states like
Pennsylvania may well show

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:20.926
early leads for the president
based on the same-day vote.

00:04:20.926 --> 00:04:24.330
That would be before mail-in
ballots where Democrats

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.632
are expected to have
an advantage in Pennsylvania

00:04:26.632 --> 00:04:28.000
are counted.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:31.070
-I think it's terrible when
we can't know the results

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:32.871
of an election the night
of the election

00:04:32.871 --> 00:04:34.940
in a modern day age
of computers.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:36.909
I think it's a terrible thing.

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:39.344
We're going to go in
the night of.

00:04:39.344 --> 00:04:41.080
As soon as that election
is over,

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:43.081
we're going in with our lawyers.

00:04:43.081 --> 00:04:45.384
-First of all, do you even have
any lawyers left?

00:04:45.384 --> 00:04:47.286
Most of them have quit,
gone to jail,

00:04:47.286 --> 00:04:48.821
or have been tricked by Borat.

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:50.456
If you're going to need Rudy
on election night,

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:53.025
give him a head's up now so he
can start tucking in his shirt.

00:04:53.025 --> 00:04:54.660
[ As Giuliani ] Hold on.
I gotta lay down on the bed,

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:56.695
then roll onto the floor,
then crawl to the phone

00:04:56.695 --> 00:04:58.264
to call someone to help me up.

00:04:58.264 --> 00:05:01.300
I usually call my cousin,
AKA, my wife!

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:03.903
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.903 --> 00:05:05.838
Secondly,
you never know the official --

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:07.940
What?
Still works on Shoemaker, guys.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:10.143
I got a very small sample size

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:12.945
to know these callbacks
are working.

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:14.280
Second, we never know

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:16.081
the official final results
on election night.

00:05:16.081 --> 00:05:18.484
Those are just projections based
on partial vote counts.

00:05:18.484 --> 00:05:20.686
Election day itself is mostly
an invention of TV

00:05:20.686 --> 00:05:21.887
and radio, like jingles.

00:05:21.887 --> 00:05:24.123
Before radio and TV,
no one ever gave you

00:05:24.123 --> 00:05:25.858
their telephone number via song.

00:05:25.858 --> 00:05:27.226
"Can I call you some time?"

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:30.263
"Sure. My number is
♪ K-A-R-S, Kars For Kids" ♪

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:31.497
"You know what? Just say no.

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:33.298
If you don't want me
to call you, just say no."

00:05:33.298 --> 00:05:35.367
The actual votes are tallied
and then certified

00:05:35.367 --> 00:05:36.836
days or weeks
after the election,

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:39.572
and then the electoral college
meets in December

00:05:39.572 --> 00:05:42.108
to make it official.
That's always how it's worked.

00:05:42.108 --> 00:05:43.776
That's why presidential
inaugurations

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:45.077
used to be in March.

00:05:45.077 --> 00:05:47.279
Back in the day, it took so long
to find out who won,

00:05:47.279 --> 00:05:50.583
one guy became President
and then immediately died.

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:52.651
Somebody should do a musical
about that guy.

00:05:52.651 --> 00:05:54.420
♪ My name
is William Henry Harrison ♪

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:55.521
Oh [bleep] it works.

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:57.223
Oh, Broadway, here we come.

00:05:57.223 --> 00:05:58.991
What? Why not?

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:00.025
Closed, why?

00:06:00.025 --> 00:06:02.528
Oh, right. The pandemic.

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:04.463
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:04.463 --> 00:06:06.532
-they're making their strategy
as clear as they can.

00:06:06.532 --> 00:06:08.834
Republicans have been in court
desperately trying to throw out

00:06:08.834 --> 00:06:10.703
ballots in states like Texas,
Wisconsin,

00:06:10.703 --> 00:06:11.937
Minnesota, and Pennsylvania.

00:06:11.937 --> 00:06:13.973
They're not just saying
the quiet part loud.

00:06:13.973 --> 00:06:15.274
They're screaming it.
On Sunday,

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:18.277
Trump campaign officials
and overinflated football

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:21.247
Jason Miller lied about the vote
counting process

00:06:21.247 --> 00:06:24.216
and said that if Trump seems to
be ahead on election night,

00:06:24.216 --> 00:06:26.486
he'll prematurely declare
victory and try to stop

00:06:26.486 --> 00:06:28.121
the remaining ballots
from being counted.

00:06:28.121 --> 00:06:30.055
-If you speak with many
smart Democrats,

00:06:30.055 --> 00:06:32.257
they believe that
President Trump will be ahead

00:06:32.257 --> 00:06:35.227
on election night, probably
getting 280 electorals,

00:06:35.227 --> 00:06:37.130
somewhere in that range,
and then they're going try

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:38.764
to steal it back after
the election.

00:06:38.764 --> 00:06:40.333
-By steal it back, you mean

00:06:40.333 --> 00:06:42.468
count all the votes,
you Funko Pop!?

00:06:42.468 --> 00:06:45.237
There is no magic cutoff where
you guys get to suddenly

00:06:45.237 --> 00:06:46.839
just decide the election
is over.

00:06:46.839 --> 00:06:48.574
If you could just declare
yourself the winner

00:06:48.574 --> 00:06:50.876
whenever you're ahead,
the jets wouldn't be 0-8.

00:06:50.876 --> 00:06:53.346
They would be a still terrible
2-6.

00:06:53.346 --> 00:06:55.247
TV news networks have to be
careful with this

00:06:55.247 --> 00:06:56.815
because it's extremely
dangerous.

00:06:56.815 --> 00:06:58.650
We have to be prepared
as a nation

00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:01.320
for early returns in places like
Pennsylvania, Michigan,

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:04.156
Wisconsin, and Minnesota
to differ significantly

00:07:04.156 --> 00:07:06.892
from final vote tallies
as mail ballots are counted.

00:07:06.892 --> 00:07:09.228
Even if Biden wins Pennsylvania
by five points,

00:07:09.228 --> 00:07:11.830
as the polls currently suggest,
a disproportionate number

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:14.667
of Democratic mail-in votes
means we could be in a situation

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:17.636
where trump is ahead by as much
as 16 points on election night.

00:07:17.636 --> 00:07:20.038
And if that happens, you know
he is going to run out onstage

00:07:20.038 --> 00:07:21.873
and declare himself the winner
and barricade himself

00:07:21.873 --> 00:07:24.243
in the White House with
a year's supply of Diet Coke

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:25.911
and three to five Melanias.

00:07:25.911 --> 00:07:28.080
[ As Trump ] My favorite
is Morpheus Melania.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:31.684
And my least favorite is the one
who won't hold my hand!

00:07:31.684 --> 00:07:33.719
[ Normal voice ] Which is why
if Trump decides to just

00:07:33.719 --> 00:07:36.355
declare victory, TV networks
should refuse to air it,

00:07:36.355 --> 00:07:38.858
or at the very least make clear
that it's meaningless.

00:07:38.858 --> 00:07:40.559
You can't just declare yourself
President

00:07:40.559 --> 00:07:41.827
any more than I can go to
the mall

00:07:41.827 --> 00:07:44.029
and declare my dad New
Hampshire's sexiest man.

00:07:44.029 --> 00:07:46.932
Though, tell me I'm wrong.

00:07:46.932 --> 00:07:48.367
There is virtually no dispute

00:07:48.367 --> 00:07:50.203
about who is actually going to
win more votes.

00:07:50.203 --> 00:07:52.705
So this is all Trump and his
allies have left -- cheating.

00:07:52.705 --> 00:07:55.041
The president and Republican
party have left the nation

00:07:55.041 --> 00:07:58.210
in tatters after four years of
crisis, incompetence, and greed,

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:00.045
so they have nothing to run on,
which is why they built

00:08:00.045 --> 00:08:02.515
their entire campaign strategy
around whipping up fear

00:08:02.515 --> 00:08:04.850
and calling anyone who opposes
them an angry mob.

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:07.987
-It is clear the media mob
is full of liars.

00:08:07.987 --> 00:08:10.723
The media mob, of course,
aiding and abetting

00:08:10.723 --> 00:08:12.458
and protecting fragile Joe.

00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:15.127
-They have decided to be
activists for the left-wing mob.

00:08:15.127 --> 00:08:18.164
-Right now the mob has a voice
in the Democrat Party.

00:08:18.164 --> 00:08:20.799
-Joe Biden capitulated to
the radical left-wing mob.

00:08:20.799 --> 00:08:24.002
-Biden's strategy is to
surrender to the left-wing mob.

00:08:24.002 --> 00:08:26.305
He wants to surrender
your nation

00:08:26.305 --> 00:08:29.241
to the radical left-wing mob.

00:08:29.241 --> 00:08:31.910
There is only one thing standing
between your family

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:33.712
and the radical left-wing mob.

00:08:33.712 --> 00:08:35.848
-First of all, I'm not sure
I would use the word "mob"

00:08:35.848 --> 00:08:37.749
when your guy dresses like
he just got done

00:08:37.749 --> 00:08:39.284
strangling Luca Brasi.

00:08:39.284 --> 00:08:41.553
Looks like he's about to pour
kerosene on an informant

00:08:41.553 --> 00:08:42.821
tied up in the basement.

00:08:42.821 --> 00:08:45.324
[ As Trump ] So hard
to get the smell of gas

00:08:45.324 --> 00:08:46.625
out of fine Italian leather.

00:08:46.625 --> 00:08:49.662
And have I Pavarotti tickets
tonight.

00:08:49.662 --> 00:08:52.030
He likes me,
for whatever reason.

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:53.599
[ Normal voice ] But the reality
of course is the Trump

00:08:53.599 --> 00:08:55.167
and his allies don't hate mobs
at all.

00:08:55.167 --> 00:08:57.135
In fact, they like them plenty
when they're the ones

00:08:57.135 --> 00:08:59.772
forming the mob, as we saw
in Texas on Friday.

00:08:59.772 --> 00:09:02.308
-A campaign confrontation
on a Texas highway.

00:09:02.308 --> 00:09:04.576
A caravan of President Trump
supporters

00:09:04.576 --> 00:09:07.779
surrounded a Biden-Harris bus
as it was traveling

00:09:07.779 --> 00:09:10.082
from San Antonio to Austin
Friday.

00:09:10.082 --> 00:09:12.885
A Biden campaign official says
the vehicles tried to slow

00:09:12.885 --> 00:09:16.055
the bus down and even
push it off the road.

00:09:16.055 --> 00:09:19.024
-911 was called by people inside
the bus,

00:09:19.024 --> 00:09:21.861
and tonight the FBI has
confirmed to NBC News

00:09:21.861 --> 00:09:23.929
it is investigating that
incident.

00:09:23.929 --> 00:09:27.033
-The President just moments
ago tweeted this in reply.

00:09:30.169 --> 00:09:32.237
-There is a Biden bus,
and it's surrounded

00:09:32.237 --> 00:09:36.409
by pickup trucks on a highway,
all with Trump signs.

00:09:36.409 --> 00:09:38.343
I mean, it is ordinary Americans

00:09:38.343 --> 00:09:41.881
just taking this election
into their own hands.

00:09:41.881 --> 00:09:46.085
-Listen, I saw yesterday a
video of these people in Texas.

00:09:46.085 --> 00:09:49.355
Did you see it?
All the cars on the road.

00:09:49.355 --> 00:09:51.323
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:51.323 --> 00:09:54.093
We love what they did, but here
is the thing they don't know.

00:09:54.093 --> 00:09:56.295
We do that in Florida every day.

00:09:56.295 --> 00:09:59.265
-You see the way our people,
they were protecting

00:09:59.265 --> 00:10:01.967
this bus yesterday,
because they're nice.

00:10:01.967 --> 00:10:03.902
-Yeah, sure, they were
protecting the bus.

00:10:03.902 --> 00:10:06.438
The same way a loan shark
helps you find your wallet.

00:10:06.438 --> 00:10:08.974
Cool shout out to his home state
from Rubio there --

00:10:08.974 --> 00:10:11.610
Florida, we also
terrorize our buses!

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:12.911
I mean, my God, this guy.

00:10:12.911 --> 00:10:14.980
"How did I do, Mr. President?
You like my speech?"

00:10:14.980 --> 00:10:16.214
[ As Trump ]
[Bleep] off, little Marco.

00:10:16.214 --> 00:10:17.650
Have some respect for yourself.

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:20.185
[ Laughter ]

00:10:20.185 --> 00:10:22.320
The constant cheating,
threats of physical violence,

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:24.490
in addition to be terrifying,
it's also exhausting,

00:10:24.490 --> 00:10:27.326
which is why we've all been
anxiously awaiting this moment

00:10:27.326 --> 00:10:28.761
for four years,
and for that reason,

00:10:28.761 --> 00:10:30.295
it feels surreal
to finally be here.

00:10:30.295 --> 00:10:32.464
I probably started thinking
about the 2020 election

00:10:32.464 --> 00:10:34.767
the moment Trump was declared
the winner in 2016.

00:10:34.767 --> 00:10:37.636
And judging from Trump's face
that night, I wasn't alone.

00:10:37.636 --> 00:10:40.305
Wow, it's like when the teacher
says "Oral reports are today,

00:10:40.305 --> 00:10:43.109
and just for kicks, let's go
in reverse alphabetical order."

00:10:43.109 --> 00:10:44.409
That's him after he asked...

00:10:44.409 --> 00:10:46.312
[ As Trump ] Oh, God.
How long is this job anyway?

00:10:46.312 --> 00:10:48.747
A months? Six weeks?
Four years?!

00:10:48.747 --> 00:10:50.215
Is that human years,
or dog years?

00:10:50.215 --> 00:10:51.950
Before you answer, which one
is longer?

00:10:51.950 --> 00:10:53.252
[ Normal voice ] And now
we're finally here,

00:10:53.252 --> 00:10:55.254
and the final days of Trump's
campaign has predictably

00:10:55.254 --> 00:10:56.989
turned vicious and ugly
with his supporters

00:10:56.989 --> 00:10:58.791
calling for virtually anyone
who opposes Trump

00:10:58.791 --> 00:11:01.293
to be in prison from Joe Biden
to Hillary Clinton

00:11:01.293 --> 00:11:03.762
to Gretchen Whitmer,
to Ilhan Omar.

00:11:03.762 --> 00:11:08.567
-Joe Biden is a corrupt
politician

00:11:08.567 --> 00:11:10.269
who bought and is paid for.

00:11:10.269 --> 00:11:13.072
Look, he is bought and paid for
by China.

00:11:13.072 --> 00:11:15.540
How about his son?
His son walks in.

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:17.243
He is supposed to be fair.

00:11:20.979 --> 00:11:23.782
This place was a mess
four years ago, and frankly,

00:11:23.782 --> 00:11:26.986
if your governor opened up
your state --

00:11:26.986 --> 00:11:28.788
[ Crowd booing ]

00:11:32.491 --> 00:11:35.394
You think Ilhan Omar,
that's one of the reasons

00:11:35.394 --> 00:11:38.363
we're going win Minnesota,
because of Ilhan Omar.

00:11:38.363 --> 00:11:41.267
Didn't she harvest?
I heard she ballot harvested,

00:11:41.267 --> 00:11:42.334
didn't she?

00:11:42.334 --> 00:11:44.436
So where is
our justice department?

00:11:44.436 --> 00:11:47.439
In fact crazy Hillary,
crooked Hillary came in.

00:11:47.439 --> 00:11:49.975
[ Crowd booing ]
Here we go. Watch.

00:11:49.975 --> 00:11:51.843
There we go.

00:11:51.843 --> 00:11:54.212
They always blame me.
Whenever that chant starts,

00:11:54.212 --> 00:11:56.015
all I do is I mention her name.

00:12:00.019 --> 00:12:02.220
-But, sure, the Democrats
are an angry mob.

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:04.290
There is only one side in this
race that encourages

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:05.891
their supporters to scream
"Lock them up!"

00:12:05.891 --> 00:12:07.192
about anyone they don't like.

00:12:07.192 --> 00:12:08.626
They sound like
they should be holding torches

00:12:08.626 --> 00:12:09.962
and chasing Frankenstein.

00:12:09.962 --> 00:12:12.531
"Lock him up in the castle
with Zombie Pavarotti!"

00:12:12.531 --> 00:12:14.700
At what point can we just call
this fascism?

00:12:14.700 --> 00:12:16.769
And by the way, to the people
who think calling Trump

00:12:16.769 --> 00:12:18.637
a fascist is left-wing hysteria,

00:12:18.637 --> 00:12:21.306
you can be a fascist without
being Hitler or Mussolini

00:12:21.306 --> 00:12:23.008
the same way you can be
a basketball player

00:12:23.008 --> 00:12:24.843
without being LeBron James
or Michael Jordan

00:12:24.843 --> 00:12:27.780
or, hell, Barack Obama.

00:12:38.224 --> 00:12:40.559
[ Laughter ]

00:12:40.559 --> 00:12:43.129
-Come on.

00:12:44.663 --> 00:12:46.898
-Nothing summarizes
the Democrats right now

00:12:46.898 --> 00:12:47.833
more than that clip.

00:12:47.833 --> 00:12:49.335
"Yeah, that's our guy!"

00:12:49.335 --> 00:12:50.469
"The one who made the shot?"

00:12:50.469 --> 00:12:53.472
"No, no, the "All net" guy.

00:12:53.472 --> 00:12:56.108
"Oh. That's good, too."

00:12:56.108 --> 00:12:58.076
Anyway, the point is
the president is closing out

00:12:58.076 --> 00:12:59.879
an ugly and vicious four years
of the series

00:12:59.879 --> 00:13:02.281
of ugly and vicious rallies.
But when he is not revved up,

00:13:02.281 --> 00:13:04.517
calling for the imprisonment
of his political opponents

00:13:04.517 --> 00:13:06.619
or for valid votes to be tossed
out,

00:13:06.619 --> 00:13:08.487
he seems to lose a lot of steam.

00:13:08.487 --> 00:13:11.857
Pennsylvania on Saturday, he was
so, dare I say, low energy,

00:13:11.857 --> 00:13:14.860
he almost seemed like a man
who knew he was going to lose.

00:13:14.860 --> 00:13:16.595
-[ Hoarse voice ]
They hate what they're seeing

00:13:16.595 --> 00:13:21.967
because they're not looking at
fake suppression polls anymore.

00:13:21.967 --> 00:13:25.370
Now they're looking at the
numbers that are pouring in.

00:13:25.370 --> 00:13:27.839
And they don't like the numbers
that they're seeing

00:13:27.839 --> 00:13:32.911
in Florida and in Ohio
and in North Carolina.

00:13:32.911 --> 00:13:35.447
It could have been
the greatest --

00:13:35.447 --> 00:13:37.082
You know, if you look,

00:13:37.082 --> 00:13:40.885
we look at the amount of money
that he has raised.

00:13:40.885 --> 00:13:44.289
Hundreds of millions,
$300 million one month.

00:13:44.289 --> 00:13:46.525
But I could have been
the greatest of all time.

00:13:46.525 --> 00:13:49.595
-Yeesh! Did he eat
an entire Thanksgiving turkey

00:13:49.595 --> 00:13:51.029
before the speech?

00:13:51.029 --> 00:13:52.731
Was it cooked?

00:13:52.731 --> 00:13:54.833
He sounds like your burnt out
uncle falling asleep

00:13:54.833 --> 00:13:56.668
on the couch
of the Lions-Bears game.

00:13:56.668 --> 00:13:58.103
[ As Trump, sleepy voice ]
You know I played football

00:13:58.103 --> 00:13:59.405
in high school.

00:13:59.405 --> 00:14:02.374
I was going to go pro until
I broke my tailbone

00:14:02.374 --> 00:14:05.810
in a butt-chugging accident.

00:14:05.810 --> 00:14:08.247
Could have been the greatest
of all ti...

00:14:08.247 --> 00:14:09.782
all time.

00:14:09.782 --> 00:14:10.683
[ Normal voice ] Look, I get it.

00:14:10.683 --> 00:14:12.050
Trump is tired. We all are.

00:14:12.050 --> 00:14:13.652
One of the many things you
can say about the Trump era

00:14:13.652 --> 00:14:15.720
and about this campaign
is it's been exhausting.

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:18.690
Just four years of constant
crises, late-breaking news,

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:20.025
midnight votes,
and 3:00 a.m. tweets.

00:14:20.025 --> 00:14:22.627
In fact, on Friday, Trump
scream-tweeted yet another

00:14:22.627 --> 00:14:25.798
incoherent rant which implied
that he wants the Supreme Court

00:14:25.798 --> 00:14:27.932
to stop the counting of mail
ballots to help him win.

00:14:27.932 --> 00:14:30.235
-President Trump tweeted this
morning that if Biden

00:14:30.235 --> 00:14:33.271
is elected, the four justices
that voted in favor

00:14:33.271 --> 00:14:37.142
of the ballot extension would be
relegated to sitting on

00:14:37.142 --> 00:14:41.780
not only a heavily packed court,
but probably a revolving court.

00:14:41.780 --> 00:14:45.850
He said at least the many new
justices will be radical left.

00:14:45.850 --> 00:14:47.953
-I don't know what's crazier,
that the president tweeted that

00:14:47.953 --> 00:14:50.990
at 2:57 a.m., or the first time
I read "plus1,"

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:53.024
I assumed it was him
trying to spell "Pelosi."

00:14:53.024 --> 00:14:55.160
Trump can't run on reality,
so he has to run against it

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:57.262
because the reality is
that after four years

00:14:57.262 --> 00:14:59.198
of serial cruelties,
absurdities, lies,

00:14:59.198 --> 00:15:01.400
and abusive power,
he's left the nation in ruins.

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:03.501
Half a million new COVID cases
in just one week,

00:15:03.501 --> 00:15:04.970
hospital ICUs filling up,

00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:06.438
8 million new people in poverty,

00:15:06.438 --> 00:15:08.707
a quarter of all households
struggling with food insecurity,

00:15:08.707 --> 00:15:11.009
tens of millions facing eviction
and homelessness,

00:15:11.009 --> 00:15:12.811
wildfires supercharged
by climate change,

00:15:12.811 --> 00:15:14.546
civil unrest over systemic
racism,

00:15:14.546 --> 00:15:16.114
protesters brutalized by police,

00:15:16.114 --> 00:15:17.749
federal agents tear gassing
protesters

00:15:17.749 --> 00:15:19.318
and snatching them
in unmarked cars,

00:15:19.318 --> 00:15:21.253
armed right-wing gunmen
patrolling the streets,

00:15:21.253 --> 00:15:22.654
migrant families ripped apart,

00:15:22.654 --> 00:15:25.123
children who are still missing
their parents to this day,

00:15:25.123 --> 00:15:26.858
a postal service near collapse,

00:15:26.858 --> 00:15:29.060
weird handshakes and flag hugs,

00:15:29.060 --> 00:15:30.595
umbrella ditching
and dance moves

00:15:30.595 --> 00:15:32.697
where he looks like a tortoise
flipped on its back,

00:15:32.697 --> 00:15:34.700
and a president so soulless
and corrupt he's fought with

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:36.835
Gold Star families,
called war heroes "losers,"

00:15:36.835 --> 00:15:38.570
been impeached, had multiple
lawyers, aides,

00:15:38.570 --> 00:15:39.838
and campaign chairmen indicted,

00:15:39.838 --> 00:15:42.107
faced at least 26 allegations
of sexual assault,

00:15:42.107 --> 00:15:44.043
obstructed justice,
broke election laws

00:15:44.043 --> 00:15:45.544
by paying hush money
to a porn star,

00:15:45.544 --> 00:15:47.846
extorted a foreign country,
had his charity dissolved,

00:15:47.846 --> 00:15:49.214
tax returns subpoenaed,

00:15:49.214 --> 00:15:51.816
had a secret Chinese bank
account while he was president,

00:15:51.816 --> 00:15:53.685
paid $750 in taxes,

00:15:53.685 --> 00:15:55.487
and bilked taxpayers
out of $8 million,

00:15:55.487 --> 00:15:58.056
including $3
for a glass of water.

00:15:58.056 --> 00:15:59.657
Maybe that is why he is always
so careful with it.

00:15:59.657 --> 00:16:02.127
[ As Trump ] Can't spill any.
Every drop cost 50 cents!

00:16:02.127 --> 00:16:03.295
[ Normal voice ]
And on top of everything else,

00:16:03.295 --> 00:16:04.896
he forgot the words
to the national anthem

00:16:04.896 --> 00:16:06.564
and "God Bless America."

00:16:06.564 --> 00:16:11.036
-♪ What so proudly we hailed ♪

00:16:11.036 --> 00:16:16.075
♪ At the twilight's
last gleaming ♪

00:16:16.075 --> 00:16:19.544
-♪ Land that I love ♪

00:16:19.544 --> 00:16:24.015
♪ Stand beside her
and guide her ♪

00:16:24.015 --> 00:16:25.884
-The president
of the United States

00:16:25.884 --> 00:16:27.585
sings our most patriotic songs

00:16:27.585 --> 00:16:29.721
like a lapsed Catholic
faking their way

00:16:29.721 --> 00:16:31.657
through the call and response
at Easter mass.

00:16:31.657 --> 00:16:34.292
"In the name of the father,
the son, and the holy spirit.

00:16:34.292 --> 00:16:38.430
[ As Trump ] Boo-yah?

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:40.899
[ Whispering ] It's "boo-yah."
Is it not "boo-yah"?

00:16:40.899 --> 00:16:43.202
[ Normal voice ] This is it.
This is our chance to put an end

00:16:43.202 --> 00:16:44.669
to the cruelty,
the abuses of power,

00:16:44.669 --> 00:16:45.871
and the criminal neglect.

00:16:45.871 --> 00:16:47.473
Trump incites violence
and threatens to cheat

00:16:47.473 --> 00:16:49.541
because he wants us to feel like
he is inevitable,

00:16:49.541 --> 00:16:51.376
that he is insulated
from public opinion

00:16:51.376 --> 00:16:52.677
and Democratic accountability,

00:16:52.677 --> 00:16:53.912
that nothing and no one
can stop him.

00:16:53.912 --> 00:16:56.081
Tomorrow is our chance
to prove him wrong.

00:16:56.081 --> 00:16:59.250
It's in our power to repudiate
Trump and all he stands for

00:16:59.250 --> 00:17:00.352
in overwhelming numbers.

00:17:00.352 --> 00:17:01.853
It's our chance
to save our democracy.

00:17:01.853 --> 00:17:04.089
And if we succeed,
this time tomorrow,

00:17:04.089 --> 00:17:06.457
Trump could very well
be onstage saying...

00:17:06.457 --> 00:17:07.992
-I will leave tonight.

00:17:07.992 --> 00:17:09.895
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:17:09.895 --> 00:17:13.398 line:0%
♪♪

00:17:13.398 --> 00:17:14.999
-God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:17:14.999 --> 00:17:17.403
over 2 million meals a year
to men, women, and children

00:17:17.403 --> 00:17:20.038
living with HIV/AIDS, cancer,
and other serious illnesses,

00:17:20.038 --> 00:17:21.840
and they need your help
now more than ever.

00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:24.643
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the "donate" button.

00:17:24.643 --> 00:17:28.213
Stay safe, wash your hands,
wear a mask. We love you.

